{
 "_comment": "Terrain categories: what an id of the ground control map is. Each chooses from the libraries beside this file - soils per material class (grass, dirt, sand, rock, marsh, snow; a class it does not name is its parent's, and a parent of none is the engine's own), rock on slopes and the scree at their foot, ground foliage (or none), decal sets with density weights, the layer biomes where the forest, water and decor layers say 0, a look (tint, saturation) and the values the control channels take where a map does not say (tools/assemble_controls.py reads them). inherit takes everything from another category first. derive: rules that name a category for ground no map paints (generated worlds) - first match wins. climate: what the ground stands under while an import is at its primary stage (heights only, no climate worked out): a zone, warmth 0..1, fertility 0..1 - with the moisture_bias map it decides the grass, the forest and what the ground is made of before the world's own climate exists.",
